From: "Caleb E." <158400752+FoxesRCool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:45:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 65/66] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus13: enable the Iris video
 codec

video-codec@aa00000 is disabled on the Surface Laptop 7 13.8", so it has
no hardware video decode or encode. Enable it with the firmware 0030
names for the 15": both sizes come from one driver package, and
microsoft-surface-laptop-7-firmware installs the same
qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Romulus/qcvss8380.mbn for them.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 13.8" (X1E80100) from a hw-test boot
entry on linux-omarchy 7.3.0-75: the firmware loads, qcom-iris-decoder
and qcom-iris-encoder appear, and 60 frames of 720p H.264 decode in
hardware in 0.3 s.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts    | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
index 2e35b4d..92e7b84 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -50,6 +50,17 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The video codec needs Microsoft-signed firmware. qcvss8380.mbn from the
+ * Surface Laptop 7's driver package is accepted on this laptop. It loads on
+ * first use; until then, opening the device fails.
+ */
+&iris {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Romulus/qcvss8380.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &spi10 {
 	compatible = "qcom,geni-qspi";
 	dmas = <&gpi_dma1 0 2 QCOM_GPI_QSPI>,
